<!--
  One live chat message, rendered standalone by ChatWebController and sent
  as a WebSocket text frame (M5, architecture §8's htmx-HTML-swap client
  path — see ChatRoomRegistry's doc comment on why this is HTML, not the
  shared ChatEnvelope JSON type).

  hx-swap-oob="beforeend:\#chat-messages" lives directly on the
  \#(message.id)-tagged div itself, not on an outer wrapper — htmx's OOB
  swap clones whatever element actually carries hx-swap-oob and inserts
  that clone (attribute stripped) at the target, so putting it on a
  wrapper would have appended the wrapper as an extra child of
  \#chat-messages, one level above the real .chat-message element that
  the page-load \#for loop below renders as a direct child. Found via an
  independent review that checked htmx's own oobSwap source rather than
  assuming; keeping the attribute on this element directly is what makes
  a live-broadcast message and a page-load-rendered one land in the exact
  same place in the DOM.

  The markup here is intentionally identical to the \#for loop in
  pages/event-detail.leaf that renders the initial history on page load —
  kept as plain duplicated markup rather than a shared \#extend'd partial,
  since \#extend's context-sharing behavior inside a \#for loop wasn't
  something this build could verify against a real compiler; if you change
  one, change the other.
-->
#if(message.parentID):
<div class="chat-message ml-6 border-l-2 border-gray-200 pl-3" data-message-id="#(message.id)" hx-swap-oob="beforeend:\#chat-messages">
#else:
<div class="chat-message" data-message-id="#(message.id)" hx-swap-oob="beforeend:\#chat-messages">
#endif
    <span class="font-medium text-sm">#(message.displayName)</span>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-700">#(message.text)</p>
</div>
